The `renderItem` function creates new array literals inline for the `style` prop on every render. This forces React to treat each list item as changed, preventing reconciliation optimizations.

**Suggested fix:**
Move style arrays outside the renderItem or use memoized style objects:

```typescript
// Outside renderItem
const expenseCardStyle = [styles.expenseWidgetRadius, styles.justifyContentEvenly, styles.overflowHidden, styles.highlightBG, styles.p3, styles.mb2];
const flexRowStyle = [styles.flexRow];

const renderItem: ListRenderItem<Transaction> = ({item}) => {
    // ...
    return (
        <View style={expenseCardStyle}>
            <View style={flexRowStyle}>
                {/* ... */}
            </View>
        </View>
    );
};
```

